// expect-error: never initialised
//
// A `Barrier` keeps its party count in a runtime field, not in its type, so a
// bare declaration zero-initialises it. `_zer_barrier_wait` then evaluates
// `count >= target` as `1 >= 0` on the very first caller, broadcasts, and
// returns — the synchronisation point silently does not synchronise. Threads
// that believe they are rendezvousing are not, and nothing anywhere says so:
// it compiles, it runs, it exits 0.
//
// Same shape as the unbacked Arena (arena_no_backing_store.zer); these two are
// the whole class, since every other builtin states its size in its type
// (Pool(T,N), Ring(T,N), Semaphore(N)) or grows on demand (Slab).
Barrier gate;

u32 main() {
    @barrier_wait(gate);      // returns immediately — no rendezvous
    return 0;
}
